Reason:
The bug occurs because the necessary Kerberos-related configurations are not applied before the INSTALL command is built. The first code block checks if there are any changed services, components, or hosts; if none exist, it returns early without processing any configurations. The second code block only adds components for Kerberos configuration if the state is transitioning from INIT or INSTALL_FAILED, which may not happen in time before the INSTALL command is created.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if(kerberosHelper.isClusterKerberosEnabled(cluster)) {
    // Pre-process the changed components to update any configurations
    // before tasks are created to install components
    if (!componentsToConfigureForKerberos.isEmpty()) {
        kerberosHelper.configureServices(cluster, serviceFilter);
    }
}
